    shortDescription: "The number of distinct pixels in each dimension that can be displayed on a screen.",
    detailedContent: "Resolution is a primary indicator of image sharpness. It is typically expressed in width × height (e.g., 1920 × 1080 for Full HD). Higher resolutions mean more pixels are packed into the screen, resulting in finer details, smoother text, and more realistic images. When selecting an interactive display, understanding resolution is key to matching the hardware with the type of content you intend to display.",
