    shortDescription: "Specifically refers to the physical pixel count of a monitor, TV, or interactive display panel.",
    detailedContent: "While often used interchangeably with 'Resolution', Screen Resolution refers explicitly to the hardware capabilities of the display panel itself. It dictates the maximum level of detail the physical screen can produce. For interactive panels, common screen resolutions are 1080p (FHD) and 2160p (4K UHD). The screen resolution dictates how much workspace is available; a 4K screen provides significantly more desktop real estate than a 1080p screen.",
