  article: `
<div class="glossary-article">

  <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-4 text-muted">
    <span>Published on September 17, 2025</span>
    <span>•</span>
    <a href="#" class="text-decoration-none" style="color: #0d6efd;">Touch & Writing</a>
  </div>

  <h3 class="fw-bold mt-5 mb-3" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">Definition</h3>

  <p class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #475569;">
    Annotation Tools are digital features that allow users to write, draw, highlight,
    underline, circle, or add notes directly on content displayed on an interactive
    screen. Instead of switching between separate applications or using a physical
    marker, users can interact with documents, presentations, images, and web pages
    directly on the display.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #475569;">
    On interactive flat panels, annotation tools are commonly integrated with
    <a href="/glossary/digital-whiteboard" style="color: #0d6efd; text-decoration: none;">
      digital whiteboard
    </a>
    software and support touch or stylus input. This makes it easy for teachers,
    presenters, and teams to explain ideas visually in real time.
  </p>

  <h3 class="fw-bold mt-5 mb-3" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">Why It Matters</h3>

  <ul class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
    <li>
      <strong>Education:</strong> Teachers can highlight important parts of a
      lesson, solve problems directly on screen, and explain diagrams visually.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Business:</strong> Teams can mark presentations, product designs,
      reports, and documents during meetings.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Training:</strong> Trainers can draw attention to specific areas
      of diagrams, processes, or instructional material.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="fw-bold mt-5 mb-3" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">Common Annotation Features</h3>

  <ul class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
    <li><strong>Pen Tool</strong> – Write or draw directly on the screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Highlighter</strong> – Emphasize important text or information.</li>
    <li><strong>Eraser</strong> – Remove selected annotations quickly.</li>
    <li><strong>Shapes</strong> – Add circles, rectangles, arrows, and other shapes.</li>
    <li><strong>Text Tool</strong> – Add typed notes to presentations or documents.</li>
    <li><strong>Color Selection</strong> – Use different colors to organize information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="fw-bold mt-5 mb-3" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">Real-World Examples</h3>

  <ul class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
    <li>A teacher highlights important formulas while explaining mathematics.</li>
    <li>A designer draws changes directly over a product mockup during a review.</li>
    <li>A sales team circles important numbers on a presentation during a client meeting.</li>
    <li>A trainer marks specific components on a technical diagram.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="fw-bold mt-5 mb-3" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">Benefits</h3>

  <ul class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
    <li>Improves visual communication.</li>
    <li>Makes lessons and presentations more engaging.</li>
    <li>Allows instant highlighting and note-taking.</li>
    <li>Supports collaborative discussions.</li>
    <li>Annotated content can often be saved and shared digitally.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="fw-bold mt-5 mb-3" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">Quick Tip for Users</h3>

  <p class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #475569;">
    When choosing an interactive display, check whether its annotation tools
    support multiple pen colors, palm rejection, shape recognition, handwriting
    conversion, and easy export. These features can make everyday teaching and
    collaboration considerably smoother.
  </p>

</div>
`,

